    "whatIThought": "I suspected H. G. Kane was behind the attacks, but I thought Deek might be helping him or hiding something about the house. I expected Emma’s review to be the reason she was targeted, but I didn’t anticipate how deeply the events were connected to the people around her.",
    "favoriteMoment": "The moment Deek’s apparent role as Emma’s helpful neighbour turns sinister. It completely changes how his earlier actions read and makes the story’s final twist especially unsettling.",
    "reviewText": "The premise immediately grabbed me: a negative book review leading to a real-life nightmare is such a clever setup. However it felt a bit like the start of a dramatic movie rather than psychological thriller so I dived into this book with more a mindset which left me rather unprepared for the plots and twisty writing. The isolated beach house also adds to this creating an unsettling atmosphere, and the story keeps you questioning.I liked how the book plays with the line between fiction and reality. However I think by the end it left more questions than answers and kept me wanting more from the book. The fast pacing and constant reveals make it an easy thriller to get pulled into, although the number of twists can sometimes feel a little over-the-top. Overall, it’s a tense, unpredictable read with a memorable premise. It may stretch believability at times, but it knows how to keep the suspense going."
