    "finalVerdict": "The Housemaid Is Watching builds its suspense through suspicious neighbours, hidden secrets and multiple conflicting confessions. The final twist reframes the entire investigation, showing how easily the wrong person can appear guilty when crucial information is missing.",
    "spoilerCulpritReveal": "Martha’s motive was a combination of desperation and self-preservation. She wanted the jewellery to help her escape her abusive marriage, but Jonathan’s threat to report her put that plan at risk. Rather than face the consequences, she killed him and fled.\n\nThe most important twist is that Ada wounded Jonathan, but Martha caused his fatal injury. Enzo’s apparent guilt and Suzette’s confession further complicate the investigation, allowing Martha to remain hidden. The epilogue reveals that the housemaid who seemed peripheral to the mystery was actually the person responsible for the final, deadly act.",
    "whatActuallyHappened": "Enzo initially appears to be the killer, but the truth is much more complicated. Ada reveals that she confronted Jonathan Lowell after discovering what he had done to Nico and attacked him. Suzette later falsely confesses to Jonathan’s murder to protect herself from exposure for her own involvement in his crimes.\n\nThe final twist reveals that Martha, the housemaid, delivered the fatal injury after finding Jonathan wounded and confronting him while stealing jewellery. She feared the consequences of being caught and wanted to escape her abusive husband. Meanwhile, Suzette takes the blame, and Martha remains free.\n\nJust when the mystery seems solved, the ending reveals that the person who appeared to be on the sidelines was hiding the biggest secret of all.",
