    "reviewText": "I was honestly excited to see Millie and Enzo again, but this time, instead of dealing with another wealthy family’s problems, we get to see Millie navigating her own suburban nightmare. And somehow, the neighbours manage to be just as suspicious as the people she used to work for. The beginning does a good job of building that uncomfortable feeling that something is seriously wrong. Between the overly involved neighbours, Enzo’s suspicious behaviour, and the strange discoveries around the house, there’s plenty to keep you questioning everyone. I also liked that the story shifts its focus towards Millie’s family, giving us a different side of her life. I get a bit emotional saying this but this book truly felt like a tribute back to the original. There are so many secrets and suspicious characters it just all pulls back to the first book and reminds me of why I was so addicted before. The twists are entertaining, but some of the reveals feel more shocking than genuinely satisfying, and I found myself questioning a few of the characters’ decisions.Overall, it was an entertaining return to the series, especially for someone already invested in Millie’s story. It has the classic combination of short chapters, family secrets, and last-minute revelations, absolutely amazing read thank you Fredia.",
