    "reviewText": "After absolutely loving the first book, I went into The Housemaid's Secret with pretty high expectations. Unfortunately, this sequel didn't quite deliver the same excitement for me. McFadden's writing is still simple and easy to fly through, but the pacing felt slower than I expected. The premise was intriguing, and there were definitely moments that made me curious, but I never felt as hooked as I did with the first book. I wanted that constant urge to read just one more chapter, and this time, it was missing.While there were some interesting twists, the overall experience felt a little underwhelming. Maybe my expectations were simply too high after the first book, but I wanted more suspense and a stronger reason to keep turning the pages. It was entertaining enough, but it didn't leave the same impression on me. I'll still give Millie another chance, though, because apparently, I haven't learnt my lesson yet.",
